{%- comment -%} Colour, for a screen of coloured inks (the reTerminal E1004 in its colours). A screen of grays (1bit, 2bit, 4bit) is given back its own look by the classes named for it, so it shows just as it did: a red label there is black (label--error, then 1bit:label--inverted...); a picture comes twice, in inks for the one and in black for the other. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign on_grays = "1bit:label--inverted 2bit:label--inverted 4bit:label--inverted" -%}
{%- assign inks_only = "1bit:hidden 2bit:hidden 4bit:hidden" -%}
{%- assign grays_only = "hidden 1bit:inline 2bit:inline 4bit:inline" -%}
{%- comment -%} On a magnified screen (the TRMNL X) the framework's one-line clamp lets a line that only just does not fit wrap, and its columns then run past their room: such a line stays one line. {%- endcomment -%}
<style>.screen--lg .columns .content > [data-clamp="1"]{white-space:nowrap!important;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;min-width:0;max-width:100%}</style>
